    <statement><p>Use the Product Rule to find the derivative of <m>f</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(x) = \sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x)= \sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</m>.  Then 
<me>f'(x) =  \cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)</me>








</solution>
